Subject: [PATCH] tensilelite: allow gfx906 (vega20) in SUPPORTED_ARCHITECTURES

Upstream excludes gfx906 from both lists, so `-DGPU_TARGETS=gfx906` is
rejected by `tensilelite_validate_gpu_targets()` before any code generation
starts.  This patch only opens the gate; it does NOT make gfx906 kernels
correct -- there is still no vega20 logic, and the asm generator emits
gfx90a+ directives (`.amdhsa_accum_offset`) that gfx906 cannot assemble.

Keep this as its own commit so `git revert` cleanly returns to upstream
behaviour if the P0 probe fails.

Apply from the `tensilelite/` directory:
    git apply patches/0001-supported-architectures-add-gfx906.patch
or, if the context has drifted:
    bash probe_tensilelite.sh        # it patches idempotently with python

--- a/cmake/tensilelite_supported_architectures.cmake
+++ b/cmake/tensilelite_supported_architectures.cmake
@@ set(SUPPORTED_ARCHITECTURES
+    "gfx906"
     "gfx908"
@@     set(BASE_ARCHITECTURES
+        "gfx906"
         "gfx908"
